{
 "id": "card-declined",
 "question": "What happens when a card payment is declined?",
 "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
 "recorded": "2026-10-20",
 "answer": "A declined card goes through two steps: the payments module decides whether the decline is final, and checkout then cleans up.\n\n**1. Payment layer: `shop.payments.charge_card` (`shop/payments.py`)**\n- It calls `shop.gateway.authorize`. A decline comes back as `gateway.GatewayDeclined` with a code.\n- **Hard declines** are the codes in `gateway.HARD_DECLINES`: insufficient funds, expired card, do not honor and stolen card. For these it logs a `payment.declined` event and raises `shop.errors.PaymentDeclined(code)` straight away, with no retry.\n- **Any other code** counts as temporary. It logs a `payment.retry` warning, waits for the time set in `config.RETRY_BACKOFF_S[attempt]`, and tries again, up to `config.MAX_PAYMENT_RETRIES` times.\n- If every retry fails, it raises `PaymentDeclined(\"processing_error\", retryable=True)`.\n\n**2. Checkout layer: `shop.checkout.place_order` (`shop/checkout.py`)**\nStock for the cart is reserved before the charge. When `PaymentDeclined` is caught, checkout:\n- puts the reserved stock back with `inventory.release(cart)`;\n- emails the customer through `notifications.send_payment_failed(customer, exc.code)`;\n- writes an audit entry with `audit.record(\"payment_declined\", customer_id, code=...)`;\n- raises `CheckoutFailed(\"declined\")` to the caller.\n\nBecause of this, no order is created, `inventory.commit` is never called, and no confirmation email is sent.\n\nThe docs match the code: `docs/payments.md` and `docs/runbooks/declined-payments.md`. The runbook adds two points:\n- The decline email says nothing was charged.\n- Support should not ask customers to retry a `stolen_card` decline.\n\nIt also says reservations that are never released expire after `RESERVATION_MINUTES` and are cleared by `shop.inventory.expire_stale`. That's a safety net in case `release` never runs, not part of the normal decline path. I only have that from the docs; I didn't open its code.",
